# Carom — Versus

Versus is one of the two ways to play Carom, reached from `VERSUS` on the main
menu. It is two local players sharing the keyboard, player one on the left and
player two on the right. Versus and Solo differ in who controls the right paddle:
a second human here, the AI there.

Every figure below is exported from `src/constants.ts` under the name it is given
here.

## Controls

Keyboard only. The controls are registered actions on the `LAYOUT`
(`dual-vertical`) touch layout. Register exactly the eight names in `ACTIONS`, in
that order, each bound to the keys `BINDINGS` gives it:

| Action | Keys | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `p1-up` | `KeyW` | Moves player one's (left) paddle up. |
| `p1-down` | `KeyS` | Moves player one's (left) paddle down. |
| `p2-up` | `ArrowUp` | Moves player two's (right) paddle up. |
| `p2-down` | `ArrowDown` | Moves player two's (right) paddle down. |
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` | Accepts the selected menu item. |
| `back` | `Escape` | Goes back a screen. |
| `pause` | `KeyP`, `Escape` | Pauses at any time. |
| `mute` | `KeyM` | Toggles mute. |

- Both paddles move at `PADDLE_SPEED` while a movement action is held, and are
  otherwise stationary.
- Each movement action moves its own player's paddle alone.
- `back` and `pause` share the `Escape` key. Read `pause` while a match is live
  and `back` on the menus, so `Escape` pauses in a match and goes back on a menu.

## HUD

- The two scores sit near the top of the field in monospace digits `SCORE_FONT_PX`
  (`76`) tall, drawn in `COLOR.text`: player one's score centered on
  `x = SCORE_P1_X` (`520`) and player two's on `x = SCORE_P2_X` (`760`), with
  their tops at `y = SCORE_TOP_Y` (`40`).
- The mode label `MODE_LABEL.versus` (`VERSUS`) sits small and dim, in
  `COLOR.textDim`, in the top-left of the field during a match.
